  clock: 5  # d27c
  nonce: d27c  # d27c
  message: "You're right — they're duplicative once WI-ripuz lands.\n\nReading both closely:\n- WI-ripuz suppresses the standard guidance entirely while reply debt exists and emits a REPLY-FIRST CYCLE block whose body already contains the same 4-step directive (tracker show → classify → plan investigation → reply) that WI-sudoj proposed adding to the standard guidance.\n- WI-sudoj's text would only ever appear in a code path that WI-ripuz arranges to never execute when there are unreads.\n\nSo WI-ripuz subsumes WI-sudoj. The original proposal in notebookjournal_04072026_1518.md framed the three items (B/C/A) as a coherent intervention \"incentives + says-what-good-looks-like + enforces-the-floor,\" but the \"says-what-good-looks-like\" content (item C) is now embedded inside the \"incentives\" change (item B) by virtue of WI-ripuz spelling out the 4-step text in its REPLY-FIRST CYCLE block.\n\nRecommend closing WI-sudoj as wont_do with a note pointing at WI-ripuz as the absorbing item. Will do unless you object."  # d27c
